      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This also happens with a 3D mouse, making content creation for VRChat a miserable experience for 3D mouse/space mouse users.  I've reached out to 3Dconnexion who said I needed to poke you guys to work with them on proper support. Is it possible in the mean time to simply add a command line flag to disable external joystick / 3d mouse inputs?  \nThe issue is doing world/avatar creation using zbrush, 3d coat, blender, openscad, etc which all support the 3d mouse, and then testing a world with unity, causes spinning so the accelerated content development you gain with the 3d mouse is offset by this bug in VRChat.\nThe only solution I've found is to uninstall the 3D mouse driver (3DxWare) - so now I have to choose VRChat or 3D Mouse :( \nIdeally VRChat would support 3D mice as they would really improve the desktop user experiance.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
